1 0 0 1 54 392 Tm (Clone the repository, or copy the folder, onto a Windows machine. Open a terminal in) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 378 Tm (that folder. Run vire.exe count.vire. You should see the lines 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5. Run) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 364 Tm (vire.exe greet.vire. You should see a greeting, the number 42, and the line it ran.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 350 Tm (Those two runs prove definitions, arithmetic, loops, calls, and branching before you) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 336 Tm (touch the window. Run vire.exe guard.vire. You should see two refusals, both saying) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 322 Tm (that files stay inside the program folder. That is the security test, and it should) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 308 Tm (keep failing in exactly that way. If a future patch makes guard.vire print a secret) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 294 Tm (from another directory, revert the patch.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 280 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 266 Tm (Then run vire.exe work.vire. A window opens. The title is Vire tasks. Two lines of) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 252 Tm (text are already there. The box is empty. Type a sentence and press Save. A new line,) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 238 Tm (Saved, appears in the window. Close the window. Open data/note.txt. The sentence is) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 224 Tm (there. If the file is missing, the sandbox root is not the folder you think it is, or) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 210 Tm (write was pointed at a forbidden extension. Do not fix that by disabling the check.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 196 Tm (Fix the path.) Tj
